From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sparse MLA: device-side req_id_per_token

VLLM_GLM5_SPARSE_MLA_DEVICE_REQ_IDS (default 0). XPUMLASparseMetadataBuilder
(base of the sm_80 Triton sparse MLA builder) fills its req_id_per_token
buffer with fill_(0) plus a pinned HtoD every step. One Triton launch now
derives the same int32 values from the device query_start_loc over the
whole buffer. Kept on the host path under adaptive verification (device
query_start_loc differs there).

